          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#history_of_the_idea"} History of the idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What is called
            %em Tate cohomology
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+groups"} cohomology groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi H
                    %mo ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{H}(G,N)
            associated to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tate+spectrum"} Tate spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %msup
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H N^{t G}
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spectrum"} Eilenberg-MacLane spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H N
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups"} stable homotopy groups
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi H
                      %mo ^
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %msup
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\widehat H^{-n}(G,N) \simeq \pi_n( H N^{t G})
                  \\,.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#NikolausScholze17"} Nikolaus-Scholze 17, p. 13
          %p
            What is called
            %em (generalized) Farrell-Tate cohomology
            is a generalization of this construction to possibly infinite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+groups"} discrete groups
            and topological groups
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Klein02"} Klein 02
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#NikolausScholze17"} Nikolaus-Scholze 17, section I.4
          %h2#history_of_the_idea History of the idea
          %p
            Tate cohomology was introduced in
            %a{:href => "#Tate52"} Tate52
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Tate"} John Tate
            for the purposes of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class+field+theory"} class field theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            acts on an abelian group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_0(G, A)
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^0(G,A)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi g
                    %mi g
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \mapsto \sum_g g a
          %p Then the Tate cohomology groups are
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{H}^n (G, A) = H^n(G, A)
              , for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 1
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi coker
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{H}^0 (G, A) = coker N
              , for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ker
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{H}^{-1} (G, A) = ker N
              , for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{H}^n (G, A) = H_{-(n+1)}(G, A)
              , for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≤
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \leq -2
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#Farrell78"}> Farrell78
            ), Farrell generalized this construction to possibly infinite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+groups"} discrete groups
            of finite
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/virtual+cohomological+dimension"} virtual cohomological dimension
          %p
            Later this was generalized further in (
            %a{:href => "#Klein02"}> Klein 02
            ) to any topological (or discrete) group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
